 "notes": "Claude first pass. Baseline ~148; broad gradual troughs through the first hour, deteriorating to a terminal cluster of deep wide decels (-8..0) with rebounds to 160-180 and dead toco - baseline estimate collapses to ~90 there, so shipped depths/lags in the tail are unreliable. Lates: d2, d3 (116s, near-prolonged), d6, d10 (weak toco, noted), d13, d16. d7 early (single smooth trough, nadir +15s). d8, d12 unsure (gradual troughs, contraction timing undecidable). d19 prolonged+UC (151s trough at 80-90). Terminal adds, all variable+UC: dm33 -5.42..-4.82 (nadir 75), dm34 -3.55..-2.55 (nadir 65, ~60s), dm35 -1.5..-0.7 (nadir 70) - three deep troughs the detector missed after its baseline followed the decels down. FHR largely missing -17.5..-10.5.",
